-- Messages and alerts (3f design, section 6.1): the contact point's messages, the alert channel's outbox and the
-- watcher's own state. Generated by drizzle-kit from the schema, then completed by hand below the generated part, and in
-- this first statement, which must run before anything names the role.
--
-- The role korbat_notify and its USAGE on the schema public are the superuser's to give (infra/postgres/init/01-roles.sh,
-- scripts/test-db.mjs, the README's Upgrading): the migrator does not own public and holds its privileges there without
-- the grant option, so a GRANT USAGE here would only warn, and the watcher's first statement would then be refused. So
-- the migration stops here, with this sentence, when either is missing: a half-done upgrade stops at the migration and
-- not at a watcher that cannot read a row. Two checks, one after the other: has_schema_privilege refuses a role that
-- does not exist.
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_catalog.pg_roles WHERE rolname = 'korbat_notify') THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'create the role korbat_notify first';
  END IF;
  IF NOT pg_catalog.has_schema_privilege('korbat_notify', 'public', 'USAGE') THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'create the role korbat_notify first';
  END IF;
END $$;--> statement-breakpoint
